    "### Section 1 of EDA - Temperature Stability Among the Happiest Cities in 2024\n",
    "\n",
    "In this section, we compute the standard deviation of monthly average temperatures (TAVG) for each city where data is available. This gives us a numerical measure for seasonal temperature variability, which we hypothesize is negatively correlated with happiness.\n",
    "\n",
    "We will:\n",
    "1. Clean the raw weather data, replacing 'M' (missing data) with NaN\n",
    "2. Extract monthly average temperatures (TAVG) for each city\n",
    "3. Calculate the standard deviation of TAVG to measure variability\n",
    "4. Visualize and interpret the results"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "\n",
    "# Replace 'M' values with np.nan\n",
    "cleaned_weather_data = {}\n",
    "for city, monthly_data in weather_happiest_data.items():\n",
    "    cleaned_monthly = []\n",
    "    for row in monthly_data:\n",
    "        cleaned_row = [row[0]] + [float(x) if isinstance(x, (int, float)) else np.nan for x in row[1:]]\n",
    "        cleaned_monthly.append(cleaned_row)\n",
    "    cleaned_weather_data[city] = cleaned_monthly"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "# Calculate TAVG standard deviation for each city\n",
    "city_temp_std = {}\n",
    "for city, data in cleaned_weather_data.items():\n",
    "    monthly_df = pd.DataFrame(data, columns=weather_happiest_columns)\n",
    "    if 'TAVG' in monthly_df.columns:\n",
    "        std = monthly_df['TAVG'].std(skipna=True)\n",
    "        city_temp_std[city] = std\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create DataFrame and sort\n",
    "temp_std_df = pd.DataFrame(list(city_temp_std.items()), columns=[\"City\", \"Temp_STD\"])\n",
    "temp_std_df = temp_std_df.sort_values(\"Temp_STD\")\n",
    "temp_std_df"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(12, 6))\n",
    "plt.bar(temp_std_df['City'], temp_std_df['Temp_STD'])\n",
    "plt.xticks(rotation=45, ha='right')\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Standard Deviation of Monthly Avg Temp (°F)\")\n",
    "plt.title(\"Seasonal Temperature Variability in Top 10 Happiest Cities (2024)\")\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
